  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Organisation of a visit to the Netherlands for the Indonesian government with the Indonesian Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity strengthened cooperation between the Netherlands and Indonesia on renewable energy and energy transition topics. A delegation composed of representatives from the Indonesian Ministry of Energy and Mineral Resources, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the Coordinating Ministry of Economic Affairs, and the Ministry of Industry and Downstream Investments visited the Netherlands, together with representatives from state-owned enterprises Danantara, PLN, and Pertamina, as well as Rumah Paten and Tenggara Strategics.The visit centred around a Joint Working Group with the Dutch Ministries of Economic Affairs and Foreign Affairs and included a series of meetings and exchanges with Dutch stakeholders. These engagements provided an opportunity to explore areas for bilateral collaboration, share knowledge on renewable energy developments, and showcase Dutch innovations and expertise in the renewable energy sector. The programme contributed to strengthening institutional ties and identifying opportunities for future cooperation in support of the energy transition.</narrative>
  </description>
